{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857384-interested-in-a-las-vegas-splat","id":857384,"title":"Interested in a Las Vegas splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-01T18:33:27-07:00","id":857384,"title":"Interested in a Las Vegas splat?","content":"I wanted to work on a Las Vegas based splat (since I live there or at least nearby it) but there are a lot of issues I have as a StoryTeller or a Player Character at least.<br /> <br /> 1) Our World of Darkness (the Old/Classic World of Darkness) has had a splat that is highly Mage oriented. Mages and vampires go like orange juice and peppermint toothpaste. If there are other supernaturals in this game, I should be extra careful with what kinds of supernaturals. (Demons or changelings are interesting tempters but these and Mages seem too easy to add in since this is the City of Sin we are working on, but at the same time we should be careful since playing with multiple supernaturals doesn't seem reasonable if the supernaturals are strong enough to break reality.)<br /> <br /> 2) The splat I want to make could be a potential (not direct) sequel to New Orleans or something that involves characters from that in some capacity, I have played this particular campaign twice and both times were surprisingly combat heavy (thanks to certain characters). The characters I usually make are much more social characters than combat characters. The second attempt of New Orleans has been surprisingly very stressful (a trip to the Underworld after discovering VII in town and after destroying Halleburton's ghost with a group that can't get along at all does not help. Graduating college with passing grades also doesn't help at all. Add character attachment and things get bad really fast). A game that highly focuses on working as a group could relieve stress. Making it a highly social focused chronicle would be important but having something involving mental and/or physical as a safety net would be a bonus. <br /> <br /> 3) A comedy splat would be great, and hopefully a stress-free game. A comedy of errors however would be even better since it fits with Vampire: the Requiem the best. While a lot of the 'funny moments' were not intentional by the StoryTeller of New Orleans, however, this particular piece isn't really mandatory.<br /> <br /> 4) Any characters be it not in the original New Orleans splat (a.k.a. Custom/Original characters) or in New Orleans that I want to utilize would more than likely either have anxiety/stress from seeing the Civil War and/or barely escaping the events, gone insane, or grown very cynical of events transpiring in Las Vegas. <br /> <br /> 5) My brother proposed a Gangrel Prince, specifically of the Bohagande bloodline seeing Las Vegas is known for its gambling. Covenants are very difficult to pick for control, but it is leaning either Invictus or Carthian. Trying to figure out a role for each covenant and clan in Las Vegas is interesting since a lot of my previous characters (Player Character and his 'Pet NPC's) were (barely) Lancea et Sanctum, My boyfriend's character is Ordo Dracul, and my brother was an Invictus. These previous characters are the only three player-oriented-characters from the previous game I plan to utilize as NPCs. Having them appear in Vegas needs to have their reasons. <br /> <br /> Characters planned so far:<br /> <br /> - The Prince - (S/he hasn't been named yet) - A gambit of sorts who is surprisingly rich enough to take control of a conference room in the Luxor. So far, not much is known about them except for his vice running the show. Every night they gamble on the news. Despite not being a part of the Circle of the Crone, he accepts Crone members more willingly than others in his covenant. If someone operates from a varying city under Circle auspices, he will watch them carefully. If they teach Cruac to non-Circle members, he will use Sunnikuse against them.<br /> <br /> - The Betrayed - Kurloz Hakamichi - A Gangrel (Bruja) of the Invictus. He joined the Invictus because the Prince saved his life in Chicago, then went to New Orleans and attempted to fall in line with the Sanctified (through Gabriel Hurst, the nicest zealot). He tried saving the lives of ex-coteriemates in The &quot;Big Easy,&quot; only to be continuously roadblocked until Baron Cimitere showed how he was much kinder than the other two power players.<br /> <br /> - The Scientist - Madeline Gore - An Ordo-Dracul Ventrue (Malkovian). When she was a human, she was obsessed with learning the occult and studied science the most. Now as a vampire, she is more penitent and her studies in the supernatural became more of a necessity and a chore than something that brings more positive emotions. She blames her pursuit on her death as well as her trust in unsavory sorts. She likes to play nice and hides her penitence in the facade of her joy in studying something new. <br /> <br /> - The Blushing Brides* - ((My seven characters made in <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/search/moeblobvampiremeidos\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tumblr.com/search/moeblobvampiremeidos</a>)) - Seven quiet and confused kindred, mainly Neonates, who have survived the horrors in New Orleans (somehow). Possible triggers of interest are either VII, vampire hunters, or Fae/Changelings. It just depends on where I want to go with them. One of them worked a lot with both Madeline and Kurloz (Constantine Kobayashi). Constantine has seen Madeline as 'his best friend' despite Madeline's claims of her making him suffer. While I originally played Constantine and his vampire family as Toreadors (4/7 of this group), I might make them Unbound/LeS Spina in this version. My brother said they make more sense this way and the Toreador bane won't be a nuisance. While many consider these guys their own coterie, a 'polygamous family' fits them the most. The group specifically would be 3-4 Daeva, 2 Nosferatu, A Gangrel of the Taifa bloodline and in the huge timeskip between New Orleans and Las Vegas, they would have lived in Buenos Aires.<br /> <br /> *Subject to Change<br /> <br /> If anyone has ideas to help me out, feel free to reply. There is no due-date or anything silly like that. I just want something that even a group of headstrong kindred can work with. A friendship destroying game while it is interesting is something I don't want to try on my first attempt at making a story with this system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:56:00-07:00","id":857521,"title":"","content":"Making a sequel of a campaign seems hard. It would be wise to have cliffnotes from one of the player characters (or more) on-hand to reference events therein. If such an action cannot be taken, referencing the New Orleans campaign would require reading the Ventrue splatbook to at least get an ambiguous idea of what happened. There exists a canon event for which people can default if they wish to reference New Orleans, or since the Ventrue book is but a toolkit it would make better sense to use it as such and organize events as seen fit by whatever you wish. <br /> <br /> A pattern to notice is that when a covenant is being played as a favourite, odds are the Prince is (secretly) a part of that covenant. If the Bohagande Prince has Circle of the Crone as a favourite covenant and treats Cruac as serious business, odds are he should be Crone first, Invictus second. Why would the Bohagande Prince join the Invictus as well? What motivates a gambling man to bet on and back up a particular horse? Would it be that he noticed the trend in Ventrue where the surrounding cities/provincial areas became Invictus-heavy, and joining that bandwagon seems like a good idea in the short run? There's so much of story that, for one to homebrew, they'd have to both examine outside splatbooks for what's canon, and then determine what isn't on their own merits based on the ambiguities.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help some splats give multiple-choice pasts for everybody, which could very well make adhering to canon difficult (*cough* VII *cough*).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11527-hakamichi-kurloz-sir","name":"Hakamichi Kurloz, Sir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:47:35-07:00","id":862027,"title":"","content":"I have talked with my ST and thinking on the story, I also have to think more on the role of each covenant. The Invictus and the Circle of the Crone have a strong role in Las Vegas in this story. The Carthians however are moving on up in population as are the Lancea et Sanctum and the Ordo of Dracul. How should I represent that in the characters I make? Any good character suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:52:27-07:00","id":865304,"title":"","content":"Quick Update: Because I can't think of a plot - This is going to be a standard sandbox game. My ST gave me kudos though, since he tried to make a plot and not that many people CARED about it. I hope this works since it'll be my first time storytelling AND I was considering the issues I would have with team mates. What are yout thoughts on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}